# Drafted by Gemini (R11 batch b5), edited. mori_shade's first conversation.
# Bringing back the fallen (raising..raising_closed): drafted by Gemini (docs/plans/gemini_raise_dead_mori/), the seven lines as drafted. The sum is the engine's
# raise_dead service on Mori's NPC data (data/npcs/mori_shade.json: a flat 1,000 gp for each hero, no diamond, 07:00 to 23:00); the
# services screen shows it for each hero before anything is paid, and it also opens from her menu on the map (Services). These lines are not voiced yet.

~ start
set mori_shade_met
Narrator: The scent of dried rosemary and freshly turned peat clings to the woman in black. Her white hair gleams like bone under the lantern light.
mori_shade [neutral]: Step softly, newly arrived. You stand upon ground that has welcomed many before you, and will hold many more before the moon wanes.
-> menu

~ menu
* Ask about her work as undertaker -> about_work
* Ask about the faiths of Wickermoor -> about_village
* Ask about burial and a proper rest -> shop_open
* Ask whether one of ours who has fallen can be called back -> raising_gate
* Ask for a piece of old valley lore -> rumour
* [Religion DC 13] Ask about the ferryman's token at her collar -> check_ok | check_fail
* Take our leave -> END

~ about_work
mori_shade [neutral]: When a companion falls in Druskenvald, the soil does not easily let them go. I wash the brow, fold the hands, and pay the earth its proper due.
mori_shade [weary]: Old Yorgrim down at the cemetery taught me the spade-work when I first woke here. Every soul deserves a quiet pillow, whatever they were before.
-> menu

~ about_village
mori_shade [neutral]: The Mayor's folk feed the Oak of Many Faces with blood, while the Brightsingers try to sing the dark away. I keep to the Strangers' way: we owe the Ferryman a polite nod and a clean ledger.
-> menu

~ shop_open
mori_shade [neutral]: Tell me whose memory we are tending, and we shall see them properly laid to rest.
-> menu

~ rumour
mori_shade [sad]: Do not pluck the white violets that grow round the base of the Founder's Round. Their roots drink deep from those who died without a name, and they weep on your fingers.
-> menu

~ check_ok
Narrator: She touches the tarnished brass oar pinned to her lapel, her voice dropping to the hush of river reeds.
mori_shade [smile]: You know the Vagrant's mark, then. He rowed us all across the dark water once, and he watches still to see if we waste the second breath he gave us.
-> menu

~ check_fail
mori_shade [neutral]: It is only an old keepsake from the riverbank, traveller. A reminder that every road ends at the water's edge.
-> menu

# Bringing back one of the party who has truly died: within the day's hours Mori states the terms and opens her services (the sum for each
# hero, the dead first); outside them she says when to come back. The offer stands either way (nothing is spent by asking).
~ raising_gate
if hour >= 7 and hour < 23
-> raising
endif
-> raising_closed

~ raising
Narrator: The parlor goes awful still save for the dry rustle of pages as she turns to a black ledger on the desk, smellin' of cedar and cold tallow.
mori_shade [neutral]: I do not call the departed back myself. I only go down to the water, ask the Ferryman to turn his oar, and carry him his toll.
mori_shade [sad]: He turns his oar only for souls in the water no more than ten days. They return weak and stumbling for ten days, the water's shadow clinging on.
mori_shade [neutral]: The toll is a thousand gold pieces for each soul I carry to him, whoever they were and however far they came. I keep no gems and ask no other payment.
mori_shade [neutral]: You will see the toll set out for each companion before anything is paid. Tell me whom you mean to call back to the near shore.
services
-> raising_after

~ raising_after
mori_shade [neutral]: The Ferryman keeps his ledger open, and the offer stands for the full ten days, whenever your purse allows.
-> menu

~ raising_closed
Narrator: The lamps burn low in the parlor, and a damp chill settles deep into the quiet room at this hour.
mori_shade [weary]: The Midnight and Witching hours I give to the graves, and the Ferryman takes no asking now.
mori_shade [neutral]: Come back to me from the Twilight Hour until the Evening Hour is spent. The ten days will keep.
-> menu
